699	      // every game server is reachable the moment it's handed to the customer —
700	      // "plug and play" — instead of requiring a manual PortForward from the
701	      // dashboard first. Found live: a real paying Minecraft customer with no
702	      // dedicated IP and zero forwards had no path from any public IP to their
703	      // game port at all. Dedicated IP servers need no forward — their guest
